---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import site from '../data/site.json';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Accessibility | Donovan Family Dentistry"
  description="Accessibility approach, current review status, and contact information for the Donovan Family Dentistry website."
>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Website accessibility</p>
      <h1>Designed to be usable across devices and assistive technologies.</h1>
      <p class="lead">This website is designed and tested with WCAG 2.2 Level AA criteria in mind, and accessibility feedback is welcome.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container split">
      <article>
        <h2>Accessibility measures</h2>
        <p>The website uses semantic headings and landmarks, keyboard-operable controls, visible focus indicators, text alternatives for meaningful images, labeled form controls, responsive layouts, reduced-motion support, and automated accessibility testing.</p>
        <p>Automated checks are supplemented by manual review because no automated tool can establish complete conformance.</p>

        <h2>Current review status</h2>
        <p>Chromium, Firefox, WebKit, Android Chrome emulation, iOS Safari emulation, and Microsoft Edge are included in the automated compatibility plan. A physical Android review is recorded. Broader physical-device, assistive-technology, and supported-PDF application reviews remain ongoing, and this page does not claim complete conformance.</p>

        <h2>Documents and third-party destinations</h2>
        <p>Some patient documents are provided as PDFs and may be opened by the visitor's browser or PDF application. External directions and other third-party destinations are controlled by their respective providers.</p>
      </article>

      <aside class="info-panel" aria-labelledby="accessibility-help">
        <h2 id="accessibility-help">Report an accessibility barrier</h2>
        <p>Call the office at <a href={`tel:${site.phoneHref}`}>{site.phoneDisplay}</a> and describe the page, control, or document that is difficult to use.</p>
        <p>Do not include symptoms, diagnoses, medications, insurance identifiers, or other protected health information in a general website message.</p>
        <p><strong>Last reviewed:</strong> August 13, 2026</p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
